WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.500
Why does a sad song feel so

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.400
good? An ancient Indian book on

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.310
theatre has an answer.

4
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.520
Rasa means taste.

5
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.800
The Natyashastra, ascribed to

6
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.520
Bharata, says rasa is so called

7
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.530
because it can be tasted.

8
00:00:17.081 --> 00:00:18.941
Art is cooked like food.

9
00:00:18.941 --> 00:00:21.381
Spices combine into flavour.

10
00:00:21.381 --> 00:00:24.401
On stage, causes, reactions and

11
00:00:24.401 --> 00:00:27.081
passing moods combine into rasa.

12
00:00:27.081 --> 00:00:29.021
Bharata explained art with a

13
00:00:29.021 --> 00:00:29.821
kitchen.

14
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.537
Eight tastes.

15
00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:33.457
Shringara, love.

16
00:00:33.457 --> 00:00:35.937
Hasya, laughter.

17
00:00:35.937 --> 00:00:36.847
Karuna, sorrow.

18
00:00:36.847 --> 00:00:38.877
Raudra, fury.

19
00:00:38.877 --> 00:00:39.987
Vira, courage.

20
00:00:39.987 --> 00:00:41.577
Bhayanaka, terror.

21
00:00:41.577 --> 00:00:42.897
Bibhatsa, disgust.

22
00:00:42.897 --> 00:00:44.547
Adbhuta, wonder.

23
00:00:45.363 --> 00:00:47.583
We taste, we don't suffer.

24
00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:49.763
The audience sees sorrow

25
00:00:49.763 --> 00:00:52.603
represented, tastes it, and goes

26
00:00:52.603 --> 00:00:53.693
home satisfied.

27
00:00:54.604 --> 00:00:56.724
Four grow from four.

28
00:00:56.724 --> 00:00:58.824
Laughter comes from love, the

29
00:00:58.824 --> 00:00:59.724
book says.

30
00:00:59.724 --> 00:01:01.944
A mimicry of love is comic.

31
00:01:01.944 --> 00:01:03.604
Which explains a great many

32
00:01:03.604 --> 00:01:05.274
romantic comedies.

33
00:01:05.693 --> 00:01:06.493
The ninth:

34
00:01:06.493 --> 00:01:09.433
peace. Later writers on poetics

35
00:01:09.433 --> 00:01:11.573
added one more rasa:

36
00:01:11.573 --> 00:01:12.953
shanta, peace.

37
00:01:12.953 --> 00:01:14.463
That makes nine.

38
00:01:15.727 --> 00:01:16.560
For GS1.

39
00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.667
The Natyashastra's eight rasas,

40
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.987
with shanta added later.

41
00:01:20.987 --> 00:01:23.147
Rasa is born of vibhava,

42
00:01:23.147 --> 00:01:26.287
anubhava and vyabhichari bhava.

43
00:01:27.177 --> 00:01:29.857
So the sad song feels good.

44
00:01:29.857 --> 00:01:32.017
We are not suffering it.

45
00:01:32.017 --> 00:01:33.907
We are tasting it.
